--------------prompt---------------
what is the QA of iterator pattern
------------AI Response------------
QA of Iterator Pattern
Maintainability → Traversal logic is separated from the collection, so changes are easier to make.
Flexibility → The same iterator approach can work with different types of collections.
Encapsulation → Hides how the collection stores its data from the client.
Reusability → The same iterator can be reused whenever we need to traverse the collection.
Simplicity → The client only uses simple methods like hasNext() and next() instead of dealing with the collection's internal structure.
Scalability → Makes it easier to add new collection types without changing the code that uses them.

